1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:10,580
Mr. Crayrat!

2
00:00:11,680 --> 00:00:14,820
Oh, good. I was just about to see if you were still at home.

3
00:00:15,480 --> 00:00:16,840
I've got a letter for you, sir.

4
00:00:17,400 --> 00:00:18,640
Thanks. I appreciate it.

5
00:00:20,800 --> 00:00:21,880
What could it be?

6
00:00:25,980 --> 00:00:27,480
A letter from Paul!

7
00:00:30,760 --> 00:00:31,280
Rudeus.

8
00:00:32,320 --> 00:00:34,520
Word is, you got into the University of Magic.

9
00:00:35,160 --> 00:00:35,600
Congratulations.

10
00:00:36,660 --> 00:00:40,020
I know we've had our differences, but I'm glad you're walking your own path.

11
00:00:40,840 --> 00:00:42,440
Alina Lise probably told you.

12
00:00:43,100 --> 00:00:45,400
But we've got a solid lead on Zenith.

13
00:00:46,020 --> 00:00:47,140
Give her my best, will ya?

14
00:00:48,540 --> 00:00:51,160
Pleasantries aside, we're in Eastport now,

15
00:00:51,500 --> 00:00:53,400
about to make the journey over to Begarit.

16
00:00:54,240 --> 00:00:57,120
It has the second harshest terrain after the Demon Continent,

17
00:00:57,120 --> 00:01:00,200
which is why I don't feel right bringing kids along.

18
00:01:01,640 --> 00:01:05,940
Instead, we thought the best course of action was to send Aisha and Norn your way.

19
00:01:06,520 --> 00:01:09,480
Naturally, we can't risk letting them travel by themselves.

20
00:01:10,640 --> 00:01:12,680
Honestly, it was a painful decision.

21
00:01:13,240 --> 00:01:14,500
I'd rather keep them close.

22
00:01:15,220 --> 00:01:18,160
But as fate would have it, we ran into a familiar face.

23
00:01:18,640 --> 00:01:19,900
A face you know quite well.

24
00:01:19,900 --> 00:01:24,740
When he offered to escort the little ones, I knew it was the right call.

25
00:01:25,600 --> 00:01:26,860
He'll be surprised to see them.

26
00:01:28,520 --> 00:01:29,940
Aisha's clever like you.

27
00:01:30,640 --> 00:01:32,020
She's got a good head on her shoulders.

28
00:01:32,860 --> 00:01:35,340
Norn, she's a little different than the two of you.

29
00:01:36,180 --> 00:01:37,480
And she kinda hates you.

30
00:01:37,800 --> 00:01:39,320
She doesn't get along with Aisha either.

31
00:01:39,780 --> 00:01:43,060
But, as her brother, please, be patient with her.

32
00:01:43,060 --> 00:01:46,240
Anyway, you get the idea.

33
00:01:46,660 --> 00:01:48,960
I feel terrible about dropping all of this on you.

34
00:01:49,280 --> 00:01:50,460
But I'm grateful nonetheless.

35
00:01:51,180 --> 00:01:52,000
Thanks in advance.

36
00:01:52,620 --> 00:01:54,080
Yours truly, Paul.

37
00:01:57,080 --> 00:01:59,240
You could cut his guilt with a knife.

38
00:01:59,740 --> 00:02:01,520
But I can tell he trusts me.

39
00:02:01,960 --> 00:02:03,220
Guess I gotta live up to that.

40
00:02:03,720 --> 00:02:05,640
I am the oldest son after all.

41
00:02:05,640 --> 00:02:07,880
Well, this familiar face.

42
00:02:08,520 --> 00:02:10,640
I wonder who volunteered for the escort mission.

43
00:02:10,640 --> 00:02:13,160
Guess we'll see.

44
00:03:44,040 --> 00:03:47,680
Hey, Sylphie.

45
00:03:50,020 --> 00:03:53,360
What's this? I hardly ever see you in such a good mood.

46
00:03:53,920 --> 00:03:56,480
Well, it's because I got a letter from my dad today.

47
00:03:56,660 --> 00:03:57,960
What? You heard from Paul?

48
00:03:58,280 --> 00:03:59,920
Yep. Sounds like they're all fine.

49
00:04:00,460 --> 00:04:02,560
Yeah? That's great!

50
00:04:03,080 --> 00:04:06,480
It is. And Paul said my little sisters are coming to visit.

51
00:04:07,100 --> 00:04:10,440
I know it's sudden, but I'd like them to stay with us if that's okay.

52
00:04:10,940 --> 00:04:13,660
Of course. That'll liven up the house.

53
00:04:13,660 --> 00:04:34,420
Thank you for this meal.

54
00:04:34,420 --> 00:04:47,880
Ah, Bliss. I can't believe I actually have a place to call home, and I get to eat with the love of my life every night.

55
00:04:48,260 --> 00:04:49,580
I owe Sylphie a thank you.

56
00:04:51,860 --> 00:04:55,660
Hey, Sylphie. Is there anything you want me to do for you?

57
00:04:55,660 --> 00:05:02,780
Yeah, teach me that spell. You know, the one you used during your entrance exam.

58
00:05:03,100 --> 00:05:09,040
Oh, you mean disturb magic, right? It's so easy. I can give you the full hands-on lesson.

59
00:05:09,400 --> 00:05:14,960
And in exchange, I can teach you some healing magic. I do dabble in advanced spells, if you'll recall.

60
00:05:15,400 --> 00:05:16,860
Great. You're the best.

61
00:05:16,860 --> 00:05:22,100
So, instead of foreplay, we ended up teaching each other magic after dinner.

62
00:05:22,700 --> 00:05:23,140
Hmm.

63
00:05:24,580 --> 00:05:29,300
That's weird. I don't think incantation-less healing works differently from other spells.

64
00:05:31,520 --> 00:05:36,000
I wonder, maybe it's because you don't know how the person being healed feels.

65
00:05:36,000 --> 00:05:43,660
She's not wrong. Attack spells are so natural to me, they're like an extension of my being.

66
00:05:44,060 --> 00:05:46,660
But healing magic? That's a different story.

67
00:05:49,840 --> 00:05:54,360
To be honest, it's a relief. It seems even you can't do everything.

68
00:05:55,020 --> 00:05:57,280
Well, you know, when you're right, you're right.

69
00:05:58,140 --> 00:06:00,000
Now it's your turn, Master Healer.

70
00:06:00,000 --> 00:06:12,100
So, I've been thinking...

71
00:06:12,100 --> 00:06:14,540
Please, not now! I'm trying to concentrate!

72
00:06:15,160 --> 00:06:19,600
When we finally have kids, do you think they'll have our knack for magic?

73
00:06:22,880 --> 00:06:26,960
Well, I guess... we won't know until we have them.

74
00:06:27,380 --> 00:06:28,100
True enough.

75
00:06:28,100 --> 00:06:31,980
Broody, I may have some trouble conceiving.

76
00:06:32,660 --> 00:06:34,020
It's my elven blood.

77
00:06:35,500 --> 00:06:41,560
So, if I'm unable to bear your children, you could enlist the help of a concubine.

78
00:06:43,560 --> 00:06:45,400
Sylphie, no! Never!

79
00:06:46,080 --> 00:06:47,920
It's not that I want just any children.

80
00:06:48,640 --> 00:06:50,680
I want sweet little reminders of us.

81
00:06:51,280 --> 00:06:53,300
I love you. For you.

82
00:06:54,160 --> 00:06:56,600
Yeah. I feel the same way.

83
00:06:58,100 --> 00:07:03,820
If this circle succeeds, we'll be able to move on to the next phase.

84
00:07:04,460 --> 00:07:07,660
Nanahoshi spent the past month drawing this tour de force.

85
00:07:08,240 --> 00:07:10,340
It's the culmination of two years' work.

86
00:07:11,900 --> 00:07:15,560
Okay. Would you mind me asking what this circle is supposed to do?

87
00:07:16,140 --> 00:07:18,500
Oh, it summons objects from another world.

88
00:07:18,660 --> 00:07:21,180
Won't cause another mass teleportation, right?

89
00:07:21,180 --> 00:07:23,680
No, it's safe. Theoretically.

90
00:07:24,460 --> 00:07:26,220
And just what is this theory?

91
00:07:29,020 --> 00:07:36,400
Based on our previous experiments, I've deduced that the larger and more complex the summoned object is, the more mana it requires.

92
00:07:37,060 --> 00:07:41,540
Think of conservation of energy. It applies to this world's magic, too.

93
00:07:41,540 --> 00:07:50,020
So, that basically means mana is responsible for most of the odd things that happen in this world.

94
00:07:50,960 --> 00:07:52,000
Ah, yes.

95
00:07:52,600 --> 00:07:58,040
When I conjure rocks in midair, I'm actually just transforming mana into stones. I think.

96
00:07:58,880 --> 00:07:59,920
Listen time's over.

97
00:08:00,760 --> 00:08:01,820
Let's get to work.

98
00:08:02,680 --> 00:08:03,100
Right.

99
00:08:03,100 --> 00:08:12,940
Hmm?

100
00:08:13,980 --> 00:08:14,940
Something's off.

101
00:08:15,480 --> 00:08:18,140
Like there's a hitch in the way the circle lights up.

102
00:08:18,140 --> 00:08:33,240
Did this thing short-circuit?

103
00:08:34,180 --> 00:08:35,980
Either way, it's not good.

104
00:08:36,780 --> 00:08:37,600
Guess it failed.

105
00:08:37,600 --> 00:08:57,040
Thanks for your help.

106
00:08:57,440 --> 00:08:58,120
You can leave.

107
00:08:58,880 --> 00:08:59,720
We're done here.

108
00:08:59,980 --> 00:09:01,120
Hey, don't sweat it.

109
00:09:01,460 --> 00:09:03,080
These things happen, you know?

110
00:09:03,080 --> 00:09:08,500
Well, if you'll excuse me.

111
00:09:15,180 --> 00:09:17,680
She's been awfully tense these last few months.

112
00:09:18,880 --> 00:09:22,160
Judging by the way she slumped in her chair, she must be pretty rattled.

113
00:09:23,680 --> 00:09:23,940
No.

114
00:09:24,720 --> 00:09:26,420
Nana Hoshi's a lot tougher than she looks.

115
00:09:27,160 --> 00:09:29,660
I bet she's big enough to take a failure at face value.

116
00:09:29,660 --> 00:09:29,760
You?

117
00:09:33,080 --> 00:09:50,600
I can't go home.

118
00:09:50,600 --> 00:09:51,840
Hey, take it easy.

119
00:09:52,220 --> 00:09:53,540
I can't go home.

120
00:09:53,720 --> 00:09:54,760
I can't go home.

121
00:09:54,760 --> 00:09:56,440
I can't go home.

122
00:09:56,680 --> 00:09:58,180
I can't go home.

123
00:09:58,180 --> 00:10:02,180
I'm right here.

124
00:10:02,240 --> 00:10:03,220
It's going to be all right.

125
00:10:07,720 --> 00:10:10,420
You've been working yourself a little too hard lately.

126
00:10:11,440 --> 00:10:12,560
Take the rest of the day off.

127
00:10:13,420 --> 00:10:13,660
Okay?

128
00:10:15,800 --> 00:10:16,800
What happened?

129
00:10:17,140 --> 00:10:17,780
I don't know.

130
00:10:17,880 --> 00:10:18,660
Is she okay?

131
00:10:20,880 --> 00:10:21,400
Master!

132
00:10:22,460 --> 00:10:22,940
Zanoba.

133
00:10:23,320 --> 00:10:24,300
Something happened to her?

134
00:10:24,300 --> 00:10:26,020
She's in real trouble.

135
00:10:26,340 --> 00:10:27,200
She needs help.

136
00:10:27,760 --> 00:10:28,900
She's fallen ill?

137
00:10:28,980 --> 00:10:29,860
More or less, yeah.

138
00:10:31,380 --> 00:10:33,720
Let's get her to the infirmary, post-haste.

139
00:10:34,140 --> 00:10:35,880
Master, please, allow me.

140
00:10:36,860 --> 00:10:37,600
Gently, no.

141
00:10:37,920 --> 00:10:38,360
Of course.

142
00:10:39,220 --> 00:10:40,260
Come then, Miss Silent.

143
00:10:42,100 --> 00:10:43,400
We're coming through!

144
00:10:43,400 --> 00:10:56,720
If that's true, it seems she hasn't been conducting research for the pleasure of it.

145
00:10:58,000 --> 00:10:59,060
I guess not.

146
00:11:02,920 --> 00:11:04,200
Hey, Grandmaster?

147
00:11:04,940 --> 00:11:06,220
You look awful.

148
00:11:06,220 --> 00:11:11,960
Yeah, I'm an ugly piece of work.

149
00:11:14,220 --> 00:11:15,340
I'll talk to Sylphie.

150
00:11:16,180 --> 00:11:18,080
Nanohoshi should come and stay with us for a while.

151
00:11:19,500 --> 00:11:21,780
In her current state, she shouldn't be alone.

152
00:11:22,400 --> 00:11:23,940
I can think of no better option.

153
00:11:24,360 --> 00:11:26,100
Would you mind carrying her home for me?

154
00:11:27,560 --> 00:11:28,220
Gladly, sir.

155
00:11:28,220 --> 00:11:28,280
Thank you.

156
00:11:28,280 --> 00:11:28,360
Thank you.

157
00:11:36,220 --> 00:11:40,380
Grandmaster?

158
00:11:40,780 --> 00:11:41,960
What is it?

159
00:11:42,820 --> 00:11:43,220
Nothing.

160
00:11:44,440 --> 00:11:46,660
So, how's Zanoba treating you?

161
00:11:47,080 --> 00:11:47,780
Real good.

162
00:11:48,100 --> 00:11:48,960
I like him.

163
00:11:49,240 --> 00:11:51,520
Yeah, he feeds to me lots of food.

164
00:11:52,040 --> 00:11:52,580
Oh, really?

165
00:11:53,380 --> 00:11:54,360
Good to hear.

166
00:11:54,840 --> 00:11:58,100
Sounds like Master gives you a lot to eat, right?

167
00:11:58,620 --> 00:11:58,920
Mm-hmm.

168
00:11:59,580 --> 00:12:03,700
Oh, I meant to say, yes, Master gives me a lot to eat.

169
00:12:04,040 --> 00:12:04,760
Good girl.

170
00:12:04,760 --> 00:12:10,840
Speaking of, I wonder if Nanohoshi's been eating enough.

171
00:12:11,580 --> 00:12:16,700
Chowing down with friends, enjoying your favorite foods, does wonders for the soul.

172
00:12:17,180 --> 00:12:19,040
Maybe she's been too focused on work.

173
00:12:20,200 --> 00:12:26,420
We're both Japanese and share a secret, but other than that, I know almost nothing about her.

174
00:12:34,760 --> 00:12:38,320
She's still asleep.

175
00:12:39,100 --> 00:12:40,540
Poor thing must be exhausted.

176
00:12:41,580 --> 00:12:44,080
I cast a healing spell just to be safe.

177
00:12:44,660 --> 00:12:45,180
Thank you.

178
00:12:45,900 --> 00:12:46,920
Sorry to interrupt.

179
00:12:47,320 --> 00:12:47,700
Mm-mm.

180
00:12:48,760 --> 00:12:49,420
Oh, right.

181
00:12:49,840 --> 00:12:51,540
I found this when I changed her.

182
00:12:51,540 --> 00:12:59,080
Might just be for work, of course.

183
00:13:00,580 --> 00:13:02,340
Well, better safe than sorry.

184
00:13:03,540 --> 00:13:05,840
Master, are there any signs of recovery?

185
00:13:06,240 --> 00:13:06,980
Hard to tell.

186
00:13:07,780 --> 00:13:10,020
Either way, I really owe you one, Zanoba.

187
00:13:10,720 --> 00:13:11,240
Nonsense.

188
00:13:11,420 --> 00:13:13,840
You're the one always taking care of me, after all.

189
00:13:14,440 --> 00:13:15,380
What about you?

190
00:13:15,480 --> 00:13:16,520
Are you all right, sir?

191
00:13:17,100 --> 00:13:17,880
What's that mean?

192
00:13:18,500 --> 00:13:21,580
Judging by your pallor, Miss Silence breakdown weighs on you.

193
00:13:24,380 --> 00:13:25,120
I'm fine.

194
00:13:25,840 --> 00:13:28,040
Just relived some bad memories, Zizal.

195
00:13:28,040 --> 00:13:30,800
May I ask of what?

196
00:13:32,200 --> 00:13:36,940
When I was younger, I had a very similar experience and shut down.

197
00:13:37,640 --> 00:13:39,580
Well, I can't say I know the feeling.

198
00:13:42,080 --> 00:13:43,660
He may not, but I do.

199
00:13:44,260 --> 00:13:48,240
If things had gone just a little differently, I may have ended up like Nana Hoshi.

200
00:13:53,360 --> 00:13:57,420
In any case, don't hesitate to summon me if you need any further assistance.

201
00:13:58,040 --> 00:14:00,460
At the very least, I have my strength to spare.

202
00:14:01,520 --> 00:14:01,960
Thanks.

203
00:14:02,360 --> 00:14:02,920
I won't.

204
00:14:06,820 --> 00:14:08,000
Are you hungry yet?

205
00:14:08,720 --> 00:14:11,900
If you want some food, Sylphie can whip something up.

206
00:14:14,100 --> 00:14:14,980
Oh, I know.

207
00:14:15,240 --> 00:14:16,540
You want some potato chips?

208
00:14:16,640 --> 00:14:17,940
You seem to like those, remember?

209
00:14:20,480 --> 00:14:21,920
I'll heat up the bath, too.

210
00:14:22,260 --> 00:14:23,800
Clean body, clean mind, they say.

211
00:14:26,340 --> 00:14:26,740
Uh.

212
00:14:28,040 --> 00:14:31,480
Call me if anything comes up.

213
00:14:33,220 --> 00:14:35,520
I thought I'd plugged every single hole.

214
00:14:36,620 --> 00:14:38,880
Magic circles are a lot like circuit boards.

215
00:14:39,580 --> 00:14:42,120
When you combine the traces and components together,

216
00:14:42,920 --> 00:14:44,240
they make a working circuit.

217
00:14:44,240 --> 00:14:47,620
But, didn't seem to matter, did it?

218
00:14:48,500 --> 00:14:50,140
That one point wouldn't connect.

219
00:14:51,820 --> 00:14:53,480
It's physically impossible.

220
00:14:55,160 --> 00:14:59,000
Which means, there's no hope I'm ever gonna make it home.

221
00:14:59,000 --> 00:15:09,180
Okay, what do you see?

222
00:15:09,980 --> 00:15:11,000
A magic circle.

223
00:15:11,260 --> 00:15:13,620
Master, what exactly are we looking at here?

224
00:15:14,480 --> 00:15:17,560
It's a drawing of a summoning circle Silent's been obsessing over.

225
00:15:18,180 --> 00:15:20,920
She got a bit stuck, so I'd like to pick your brains.

226
00:15:20,920 --> 00:15:25,660
I'm sure you're already well aware, but none of us specializes in summoning, sir.

227
00:15:26,160 --> 00:15:27,640
It's alright if it's not your forte.

228
00:15:28,180 --> 00:15:31,980
But since you come from different areas of study, you should have different perspectives.

229
00:15:32,660 --> 00:15:34,100
Take this part as an example.

230
00:15:35,200 --> 00:15:35,580
Do you see?

231
00:15:35,860 --> 00:15:37,800
Looks like the mana cuts off right here.

232
00:15:37,800 --> 00:15:40,300
Yeah, I think you're right.

233
00:15:41,040 --> 00:15:43,680
I'd wager it's supposed to connect with this part here.

234
00:15:44,520 --> 00:15:47,760
Can you think of a way to bridge the gap to get the mana running through there?

235
00:15:49,660 --> 00:15:52,680
Well, those two parts go like that, and...

236
00:15:52,680 --> 00:15:55,900
This is a tough one.

237
00:15:56,220 --> 00:15:58,080
If we redraw it...

238
00:15:58,080 --> 00:15:58,660
No way!

239
00:15:59,180 --> 00:16:00,160
We can't!

240
00:16:01,040 --> 00:16:04,040
Perhaps a compound design would achieve the results we need?

241
00:16:04,540 --> 00:16:05,540
Never heard of that.

242
00:16:06,140 --> 00:16:06,960
What do you mean?

243
00:16:06,960 --> 00:16:13,940
With the doll I'm researching, there are several layers of magical circles which combine together to produce a single effect.

244
00:16:14,600 --> 00:16:20,580
That being said, I've only just begun my work on it, so I have yet to actually draw a proper circle myself.

245
00:16:20,740 --> 00:16:21,060
Wait!

246
00:16:21,320 --> 00:16:23,580
When you say doll, you mean the one from the other day?

247
00:16:24,640 --> 00:16:25,660
Let me take a look!

248
00:16:26,540 --> 00:16:26,760
Hm?

249
00:16:27,760 --> 00:16:27,940
Hm.

250
00:16:27,940 --> 00:16:37,220
Whoever created this was a genius.

251
00:16:37,700 --> 00:16:37,960
Huh?

252
00:16:38,640 --> 00:16:40,660
I've never seen a circle like this.

253
00:16:41,260 --> 00:16:43,500
I have no idea what makes this thing work.

254
00:16:44,020 --> 00:16:46,260
Well, maybe it's just the two of them overlaid.

255
00:16:46,920 --> 00:16:48,680
No, there are more layers than that.

256
00:16:49,180 --> 00:16:51,000
It needs them all to function properly.

257
00:16:51,000 --> 00:16:53,940
But it could still move even when it was broken.

258
00:16:54,220 --> 00:16:56,080
Just what kind of circle is this?

259
00:16:56,620 --> 00:16:59,120
Well, I hardly know the details yet myself.

260
00:16:59,740 --> 00:17:03,200
However, according to the book, this circle controls the elbow joint.

261
00:17:04,660 --> 00:17:05,460
There, there.

262
00:17:05,880 --> 00:17:08,680
Genius like you will figure it out in no time, love.

263
00:17:08,880 --> 00:17:10,160
Yeah, I know I will!

264
00:17:10,160 --> 00:17:11,420
So, what do you think?

265
00:17:11,820 --> 00:17:14,180
If we use the techniques we learned from this doll,

266
00:17:14,480 --> 00:17:17,440
is that something that could help us fix the problem with Silence Circle?

267
00:17:17,900 --> 00:17:18,880
I don't know.

268
00:17:19,520 --> 00:17:21,280
It certainly seems possible, though.

269
00:17:30,580 --> 00:17:32,440
Alright, show her what we got.

270
00:17:40,160 --> 00:17:57,780
This might work.

271
00:17:57,780 --> 00:18:00,420
Of course, I can see it now.

272
00:18:00,820 --> 00:18:02,940
I never needed to stick to two dimensions.

273
00:18:04,220 --> 00:18:06,700
Even when they're drawn on paper, they still have depth.

274
00:18:06,700 --> 00:18:10,700
If I layer them, I can make as big of a circle as I need, too.

275
00:18:10,980 --> 00:18:14,120
Why couldn't I think of something that was right there in front of my face?

276
00:18:19,140 --> 00:18:19,580
No!

277
00:18:20,000 --> 00:18:20,880
All wrong!

278
00:18:21,200 --> 00:18:22,720
Wait, what about this?

279
00:18:25,240 --> 00:18:26,080
Oh, right.

280
00:18:26,560 --> 00:18:27,780
You're pretty smart, huh?

281
00:18:28,280 --> 00:18:28,860
Uh, yeah.

282
00:18:29,180 --> 00:18:30,080
Of course I am.

283
00:18:30,080 --> 00:18:30,780
I'm a genius.

284
00:18:31,500 --> 00:18:33,180
What should I do with this part, then?

285
00:18:33,560 --> 00:18:34,280
Hang on a sec.

286
00:18:34,280 --> 00:18:37,060
You could use this formula right here.

287
00:18:37,720 --> 00:18:40,080
Yeah, and this part should work that way as well.

288
00:18:40,140 --> 00:18:40,580
I see.

289
00:18:41,340 --> 00:18:41,740
Unconventional.

290
00:18:42,140 --> 00:18:42,660
Unfeasible.

291
00:18:42,660 --> 00:19:10,720
All right, I'll activate it.

292
00:19:10,720 --> 00:19:14,480
Unconventional.

293
00:19:14,480 --> 00:19:15,940
Unconventional.

294
00:19:34,280 --> 00:19:34,620
Unconventional.

295
00:19:34,620 --> 00:19:37,400
Wow. This is quite impressive.

296
00:19:37,980 --> 00:19:39,060
What is this thing?

297
00:19:40,040 --> 00:19:41,940
Maybe it's a type of glass?

298
00:19:42,360 --> 00:19:43,540
No, it's much too soft.

299
00:19:44,300 --> 00:19:45,780
It's just a plastic bottle.

300
00:19:45,820 --> 00:19:47,580
Oh, yeah. Yes!

301
00:19:48,040 --> 00:19:49,640
But it's something, at least.

302
00:19:50,380 --> 00:19:51,200
You've succeeded.

303
00:19:52,580 --> 00:19:55,720
And that means I can finally advance to the next phase.

304
00:19:56,120 --> 00:19:57,640
Layered magic circles, huh?

305
00:19:57,640 --> 00:20:02,560
If I continue to improve and develop the skill, I can probably summon anything I want.

306
00:20:04,620 --> 00:20:07,100
Sorry for what I put you through.

307
00:20:07,880 --> 00:20:09,220
Hey, give and take, remember?

308
00:20:10,060 --> 00:20:12,220
Next time I'm in a bind, lend me a hand, okay?

309
00:20:13,040 --> 00:20:14,380
Yeah, I hear you.

310
00:20:15,100 --> 00:20:17,220
Let's celebrate like there's no tomorrow.

311
00:20:17,780 --> 00:20:19,860
Come on, it'll be your treat, of course.

312
00:20:20,480 --> 00:20:21,680
Guess I have no choice.

313
00:20:22,340 --> 00:20:25,140
Okay, but after that, we'll call it even, are we clear?

314
00:20:26,960 --> 00:20:27,360
Cheers!

315
00:20:34,620 --> 00:20:49,320
Thank you, for all your help today.

316
00:20:49,320 --> 00:21:00,040
In my past life, I never went to parties like this.

317
00:21:00,620 --> 00:21:01,660
Here either, for that matter.

318
00:21:02,600 --> 00:21:08,640
But sometimes, when life tears you down, and your friends pick you back up, you get sucked into the moment.

319
00:21:09,340 --> 00:21:11,720
It's a feeling so good you never want it to end.

320
00:21:11,720 --> 00:21:16,020
How can you really live if you don't let loose every once in a while?

321
00:21:18,080 --> 00:21:21,040
Life is dark, so embrace the light.

322
00:22:53,940 --> 00:23:00,920
Is there anybody in there?

323
00:23:01,460 --> 00:23:01,860
Hello?

324
00:23:03,200 --> 00:23:04,760
Hey, Big Brother?

325
00:23:05,820 --> 00:23:08,240
You know, maybe we wouldn't be here so late

326
00:23:08,240 --> 00:23:09,900
if someone hadn't gotten us lost.

327
00:23:09,940 --> 00:23:12,480
You sounded pretty sure it was the right way too, Aisha.

328
00:23:16,060 --> 00:23:18,140
Big Brother! Big Brother!

329
00:23:18,360 --> 00:23:19,180
I've missed you!

330
00:23:22,540 --> 00:23:23,220
Rudeus.

331
00:23:23,940 --> 00:23:28,700
It's been a long time.

332
00:23:30,100 --> 00:23:32,520
Yeah? Too long, old friend.

333
00:23:33,100 --> 00:23:34,200
Welcome, Rui-Jerd.

334
00:23:34,200 --> 00:23:35,200
Hmm.

335
00:23:35,200 --> 00:23:40,460
La, ya, la, ya, la...

336
00:23:40,460 --> 00:23:41,040
M Nhà.

337
00:23:41,040 --> 00:23:47,800
Ya, ya, la, ya, la!

